3. Formal Preliminaries

3.1 Institutions and Domains

Definition 1 (Institution). An institution is a tuple I_i = (D_i, C_i, K_i, O_i, T_i, M_i) where D_i is a data set, C_i competences, K_i constraints, O_i objectives, T_i a time horizon, and M_i a decision mechanism. Let \mathcal{I} = \{I_1, \ldots, I_n\}.

Definition 2 (Domain). A social domain D_j is a region of coordinated activity. Let \mathcal{D} = \{D_1, \ldots, D_m\}.

3.2 Sociotechnical State and Observation

Definition 3 (Sociotechnical State). Let X(t) \in \mathcal{X} denote the sociotechnical state, and A(t) \in \mathcal{A} the state of AI capability.

Definition 4 (Observation Operator). Each institution observes O_i(t) = H_i(X(t), A(t)) + \varepsilon_i(t) where H_i: \mathcal{X} \times \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{O}_i and \varepsilon_i is noise. No H_i is invertible in general.

3.3 Time Constants (Illustrative)

Definition 5 (Technological Time Constant). \tau_A > 0 is the characteristic time of AI capability change. For compute, \tau_A \approx 180 days (doubling time). This value is illustrative and contested.

Definition 6 (Institutional Time Constant). \tau_S > 0 is the characteristic time of institutional coordination. We do not assign a specific numerical value. Published estimates vary widely: the Federal Regulatory Tracker reports a median of 159 days and an average of 206 days for NPRM-to-final pairing in the last 12 months ; the Regulatory Review reports a median of twelve months and a mean of eighteen months from Unified Agenda to final rule ; Mercatus reports a mean of 493 days and a median of 360.5 days ; and the CFPB-specific analysis reports a median of 114 days . These discrepancies reflect different measurement windows (NPRM-to-final vs. Unified Agenda-to-final) and different agency populations. We treat \tau_S as an open measurement problem, not a derived constant. Any numerical value used in what follows is explicitly labeled illustrative.

Remark 1. The v0.2 manuscript presented \tau_S \approx 335 days with an accompanying "median 159 days for some agencies" without adequate sourcing. This was an error of the same class H1 exists to prevent. We correct it here by labeling all time constants as illustrative and moving their calibration to future work.

