9. Evaluation Theory

9.1 Selective Prediction Framework

H-SYNC's evaluation is grounded in selective prediction rather than probabilistic forecast scoring. In selective prediction, a system may abstain on uncertain inputs, trading coverage for reduced risk . H-SYNC's U state is an abstention; its C and R states are predictions.

Definition 20 (Coverage and Risk). Over a set of claims \mathcal{C}:

\text{Coverage} = \frac{|\{c : \text{state}(c) \in \{N, A, S, V, C, R, D\}\}|}{|\mathcal{C}|} \tag{5}

\text{Risk} = \frac{|\{c : \text{state}(c) \in \{C, R\} \text{ and incorrect}\}|}{|\{c : \text{state}(c) \in \{C, R\}\}|} \tag{6}

The risk–coverage curve summarizes selective performance across operating points.

9.2 Three-Dimensional Metrics (Corrected)

\text{VerifiedResolution} = \frac{|\{c : \text{state}(c) \in \{C, R\} \text{ and correct}\}|}{|\mathcal{C}|} \tag{7}

\text{JustifiedAbstention} = \frac{|\{c : \text{state}(c) = U \text{ and } U \text{ is correct}\}|}{|\{c : \text{state}(c) = U\}|} \tag{8}

\text{FalseCertaintyRate} = \frac{|\{c : \text{state}(c) = C \text{ and } C \text{ is incorrect}\}|}{|\{c : \text{state}(c) = C\}|} \tag{9}

Definition 21 (Undefined Case). If |\{c : \text{state}(c) = C\}| = 0, then \text{FalseCertaintyRate} = 0 by convention, and the run is excluded from comparative analysis of false certainty rates.

Remark 11. The v0.2 numerator for VerifiedResolution included intermediate states V and S, which are not resolved. The corrected numerator is restricted to \{C, R\}.

9.3 Stratification

Definition 22 (Stake-Weighted Metric). Given a stake function \sigma: \mathcal{C} \to \mathbb{R}_{>0}, the stake-weighted version of each metric replaces cardinalities with sums of \sigma(c).

9.4 Co-Equal Metric

Definition 23 (Unjustified Attribution Rate).

\text{UAR} = \frac{|\{c : \text{state}(c) = C \text{ with attribution but counterfactual contestable}\}|}{|\{c : \text{state}(c) = C \text{ with attribution}\}|} \tag{10}

