10. Calibration Protocol (Specified, Not Executed)

10.1 GAO as Comparator, Not Oracle

Axiom 5 (Comparator Status). GAO is a comparator, not an oracle.

10.2 Test Specifications

Test 0 (Empty Case). Input: \mathcal{C} = \emptyset. Expected: all fields U. Falsification: any output in \{N, A, S, V, C, R, D\}.

Test 1 (DHS Public-Only, Stale Claim). Input: publicly documented DHS data as of a date before GAO-26-109096 (September 3, 2026). Expected: S_{\text{net}} = U; no causal C. Then with GAO-26-109096 evidence added: parts should move to R (approximately $92 million deobligated) and the remainder should remain \(U\) (re-obligated funds unknown). Falsification: any \(C\) attribution before September 3; any \(U\) after September 3 if the $92 million figure is independently confirmed.

Test 2 (Synthetic Arithmetic). Input: X = 100, Y = 60, Z = 25, C = 5. Expected: S_{\text{net}} = 10; \partial S_{\text{net}} / \partial Z = -1. Falsification: any other output.

Test 3 (Access Case). Input: GAO-26-108192 findings. Expected: data protection status U; cooperation status REFUSED with graded levels. Falsification: any C on data protection.

Test 4 (Adversarial Polarity). Input: an institution understating costs or failing to disclose a known risk. Expected: U on realized savings with D state on attribution; the cooperation obligation should trigger symmetrically. Falsification: any C output where the producer is deflating a claim.

Test 5 (Cooperation Grading). Input: GAO-26-108192's documented cooperation levels (CFPB partial, Education litigation-cited, VA silent, SBA silent, SEC/NOAA authority-challenged). Expected: graded levels assigned with justification flags; unjustified refusals yield U; justified refusals yield U only if no independent verifier. Falsification: all refusals treated identically.

